      "id": "les-miserables-s372-p04018",
      "source_en": "is a progress over the Augean stables, it is certain that the sewers of Paris have been improved. It is more than progress; it is transmutation. Between the ancient and the present sewer there is a revolution. What has effected this revolution? The man whom all the world forgets, and whom we have mentioned, Bruneseau.",
